## Introduction

So, **you want to become a bimbo?** Maybe you've found an instagram bimbo and you're fascinated by her style and confidence, maybe you're in the process of your own bimbofication and unsure what your next step should be, or maybe you're a complete beginner. Whatever the case may be, this guide will help you go from the woman you are now to **the bimbo doll you were always meant to be**. With that being said, let's get a few things out of the way:

- ❖ This guide is written from *my perspective*. Different people have different ideas about what a bimbo is and is not, but I define a bimbo as, "**A woman that has taken the time and effort to turn herself into a highly sexualized object of male attention**", and this guide will help transform you as such.
- ❖ With that being said, *it's your transformation*, so although this guide is meant to be followed step-by-step for maximum results, **you are free to skip any sections** if they do not align with the kind of bimbo that you want to be.

Ok, with that out of the way, let's talk about you. Before you continue, you should consider that becoming a bimbo is a serious lifestyle change:

- ❖ You'll get a lot of stares walking down the street
- ❖ People might not take you seriously because of how you look
- ❖ Your friends, family, and colleagues may look at you differently

Of course there are also many positives:

- ❖ Increased confidence (as we will discuss later)
- ❖ Increased attractiveness
- ❖ A body many women would kill for
- ❖ All the male attention you could ever want
- ❖ Improved health (from exercise)
- ❖ And of course, the social benefits of a hot bimbo body (people are nicer to attractive people)

Take some time to reflect, and if you've decided that you still want to become a bimbo then **congratulations on starting your bimbofication journey!** Continue reading for your first lesson.

