# Look Like A Bimbo

This chapter will explain what exactly goes into achieving the bimbo body of your dreams. You will get a general idea of the things that will go into looking like a bimbo before you take more specific steps in the **30-Day Bimbo Challenge**.

## Fashion

Fashion is a **beginner-friendly, fun, and affordable** way to customize your own style! Looking at clothes or styles that you like, going shopping, finding inspiration, and experimenting with your own bimbo style is not only fun, *it's the foundation of your new identity as a bimbo*. As a bimbo, the ultimate goal is dressing as sexy as possible, showing as much of your figure as you can get away with, and **being proud and unashamed while you do it**.

To achieve this, a good start is to **find some bimbos online** whose style you like and the next time you go shopping buy one or two things *outside your comfort zone* that you think matches their style. Additionally, try to slowly incorporate the following into your wardrobe:

- ❖ Crop-tops, low-cut tops, and string-bikinis
- ❖ Yoga pants, skinny jeans, and mini-skirts
- ❖ Pumps and High-heels, especially pleaser heels

How you dress (and how you *look*) affects how other people look at you, how they feel about you, and how they treat you. Most importantly however, **how you dress affects how you feel about yourself**. "Dress for success" isn't just a corny catchphrase: when you dress nicely for an interview you are not just trying to convince your employer that you're an impressive, successful woman, you are also *subconsciously convincing yourself*.

This is true for **everything that you wear** and we'll dive into the psychology of it in a later chapter, but for now just remember that *who you are as a person shapes the clothes that you wear, and the clothes that you wear shape who you are as a person*.

## Makeup

The second step of your bimbo journey is all about **makeup**. Let's face it: *every woman is familiar with makeup*, but most women find a style that feels comfortable and never change it. Due to this it's possible that you never discovered **the amazing things that makeup can do!** You can completely change the way your face looks with makeup: from contouring, to doing your brows and lashes, to the type of lipstick you put on you might be surprised at just how much you can customize your look.

--- Page 6 ---

Bright colors are the centerpiece of bimbo makeup: one of the classic bimbo looks is bright red lipstick, thick fake lashes, and bright, colorful eyeshadow. However, you can easily **experiment with this look to make it your own**, for example: bright pink lipstick, long fake lashes, and smokey eyes. Similar to fashion, makeup is **highly customizable** and your best bet for starting off is to find some inspiration. As usual Instagram is your friend, but for this one you'll also want to look into youtube for both inspiration and full-on tutorials and brand recommendations.

Don't be afraid to *mix things up* and try styles that go a little (or a lot) **outside your comfort zone**: you can go for an all-out pink look, something crazy and colorful, or even a darker, more punk-rock style. Your only limit is **your own creativity and how far you're willing to go**. I encourage you to experiment with different looks until you find something that suits your new sense of bimbo style!

## Hair and Hairstyle

Ok, so without a shadow of a doubt **straight bleach blonde hair is the golden standard for a bimbo**, but that doesn't mean that you have limited options. There are several variations of this that you can try out, including curvy and wavy styles of bleach blonde hair. You can also experiment with hair length, but for the typical bimbo look longer is better.

**'Well what if I don't like blond hair?'** Luckily for you being a bimbo isn't only about looking sexy, it's also about *loving* how you look! If bleach blonde hair isn't for you you're totally allowed to **break the trend and do something different**. You might want to try shorter hair or different or even unnatural hair colors. Don't forget that you can play around with different hair styles as well, including braids, ponytails, pigtails, buns, or even unique styles such as a side shave.

If you're not against it, I'd definitely recommend going for a long, bleach blonde look just to see if you like it, but otherwise you can try out many different hairstyles to **see what you like**. If the style you're interested in would be difficult to achieve with your natural hair you can always **try wearing a wig instead**. Also, a hair stylist can go a long way in helping you choose or achieve a new style. However, if having your hair professionally done is out of your budget, or if you just don't like the hassle you can always opt to color and style your hair yourself.

There are plenty of articles, Youtube videos, and Reddit posts out there about doing your own hair: in fact, I've included several in the resources section. Ultimately though **it's up to you** to look into new and different hairstyles and play around with them until you find something that fits **your bimbo style**.

