# Body Hair Removal

Ok, now we move into the not-so-glamorous stuff: **let's talk about body hair**. If you're like me at some point you've known someone who has let things get a bit *hairier than they probably should*. Maybe they were just really comfortable, or maybe it was a statement, but either way there's one thing you must keep in mind: **A bimbo is always smooth**. Pubic hair is ok as long as it's shaped, but other than that you're not going to want hair anywhere other than your eyebrows, eyelashes, and on top of your head. That being said, we've all dealt with body hair, so I'm sure by now you have your favorite method of dealing with it, whether it's enduring getting waxed or maybe having a shave.

Both of these are valid options, however **both methods can be time consuming**, annoying, or downright painful. Also, since you're going for the bimbo look (which inevitably means showing some skin) that means you'll be waxing or shaving even more than usual to **keep things smooth 24/7**.

Well luckily for you there is a solution: **laser hair removal**. LHR is a *semi-permanent* way to eliminate body hair. Similar to waxing, you can do it yourself with LHR products or have it professionally done, however, unlike waxing LHR will stop your body hair from growing **for weeks at a time**. Go with whatever method works best for you to deal with this small (but important) part of being a bimbo.

# Teeth Whitening/Veneers

Another important (but often overlooked) part of being a bimbo is **having a great smile with bright white teeth**. A great smile lets you take better pictures, makes people more friendly towards you, and makes you look and feel more confident.

Unfortunately for most people, normal life activities like drinking coffee or juice, or smoking **reduces the whiteness of our teeth**. Fortunately there are several solutions for this. There are many over-the-counter teeth-whitening solutions, with additional options if you would like the procedure professionally done.

Another great option are veneers. Veneers are false coverings that go over your teeth to give them a more natural shape. This can improve your smile, give you sparkling white teeth, and as a bonus **add to the fake aesthetic that you're going for anyway!**

--- Page 8 ---

# Weight Loss

At long last it's time to start talking about how to get that **sexy bimbo body!** When you look at a bimbo and think about what it takes to achieve that body your first thoughts might be of working out at the gym, running every day, or some other form of exercise, and while exercise is an important part of that bimbo figure it's actually **not the most important factor**.

As the saying goes, '**Abs are made in the gym but revealed in the kitchen**': exercise is *mainly* for shaping and toning your muscles and your body, not for losing weight. Working out *can* improve your metabolism to help you lose weight, but **1000 crunches a day will not undo the effects of overeating**. For this reason, when you're looking purely at losing weight (and then maintaining your goal weight) *you will want to focus mainly on what you eat*: specifically you want to burn more calories than you consume.

Like the other topics, you'll discover the specifics if you take the **30-Day Bimbo Challenge**, but for now just keep in mind that **there are many ways to control the number of calories you consume**. First you'll want to input your weight and height into a Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) calculator. This will give you *roughly* the amount of daily calories that you want to stay under.

From here you have several calorie control methods available to you: including keeping a food journal, drinking more water to combat hunger, or eating habits like One Meal A Day or Intermittent Fasting. I suggest **doing your research** into each method and maybe trying one or two to see if they work for you.

# Exercise and Body Sculpting

While you are on your way to achieving your **goal weight** I recommend that you begin to incorporate exercise into your fitness plan. Typically, exercise will not burn any meaningful amount of calories, but it will help boost your metabolism to help you lose weight. There's another benefit to exercise though: As you've learned, **calorie control determines your weight**, which determines the size of your waist, but it's exercise that will allow you to get that toned and shaped bimbo body.

If you're like me, that means you probably won't know much about muscle groups or targeted workouts in the beginning **and that's fine**. There are *an insane* amount of resources online to help you figure things out, and you always have the option to speak with a personal trainer who can give you a much more **personalized workout plan**. I've also listed some solid sources of information and workouts in the resources section of this guide.

--- Page 9 ---

It is entirely possible that after you have reached your goal weight and toned your body you *still* won't have exactly the slim-waisted figure that you had hoped for. At this point you may be interested to try **corset training**, in which you wear a corset while training to shape your midsection. Due to the pressure and stress put on your internal organs corset training does have the potential to cause harm, so **speak to a doctor or personal trainer** if you experience any pain.

## Lip Filler

And now the moment you've been waiting for: **let's talk about plastic surgery!** Lip filler is a *temporary* and *cost-effective* way to begin experimenting with plastic surgery. Unlike breast augmentation or a Brazilian Butt Lift, lip fillers typically cost between **$200 - $2000** and last anywhere from **6 months to a year** before being absorbed into your body.

Since the procedure is not permanent like other plastic surgery, you have the option of having the work done, taking time to see how you like it, **deciding on whether or not you want to do it again**, and deciding if you want to go bigger or smaller. Another benefit is that the cost of lip filler means that you won't have to save up nearly as much as you would for a more intense procedure.

